# Entries here have the form:
# ID
# <TAB>growth_divisor<TAB>int
# [<TAB>requires_light]
# [<TAB>grow_as_tree]
# [<TAB>growth_stages<TAB>int]
# [<TAB>mature_block<TAB>id]
#
# The int given for growth_divisor is the divisor used to calculate whether a plant should grow during a growth tick.
# The value must be a positive integer.  This value is used to randomly decide to grow in "1/divisor" growth ticks.
# "grow_as_tree" is present if the tree growth logic should be applied when growing.
# "growth_stages" gives the int describing the number of stages of growth to run within this block type (minimum is 1
#  since the block is placed and exists before a growth mutation).
# "mature_block" gives the ID of the block which will replace this once growth stages finishes.
# While "grow_as_tree", "growth_stages", and "mature_block" are all optional, explicitly grow_as_tree XOR the other 2
# must be specified..
# Note that the ID references are against item_registry.tablist but must appear in block_aspect.tablist to have meaning.

op.sapling
	growth_divisor	100
	requires_light
	grow_as_tree
op.wheat_young
	growth_divisor	12
	requires_light
	growth_stages	2
	mature_block	op.wheat_mature
op.carrot_young
	growth_divisor	20
	requires_light
	growth_stages	2
	mature_block	op.carrot_mature
